IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-terms`
IMPORT `oa1-nouns`

-- Old Age Security Act, Part I (Monthly Pension), "Pension Payable": who is qualified for a full or a partial
-- monthly pension (ss 3(1), 3(2)), legal residence (s 4(1)), the presumption when the Minister intends to waive the
-- application (s 4.1), the limits on payment (s 5(1) to (3)), withdrawal (s 5.1) and the Minister's access to census
-- ages (s 6). The amount is in oa1-part1-amount, the waiver steps of s 5(4) to (8) are in oa1-part1-waiver.
--
-- THE DAY EACH CONDITION IS TESTED (fork OA1-F1 in NOTES.md). The Act tests the residence periods "prior to" or
-- "immediately preceding" the day on which the person's application is approved, and says nothing of the day on
-- which "has attained sixty-five years of age" is tested. It is taken on the same day, the day of approval.
-- Residence in Canada, presence in Canada and legal residence are explained by Regulations ss 21 and 22
-- (piece oa3); here the person states the result as a fact.

§ `Pension Payable`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 3(1): who may be paid a full monthly pension

-- July 1, 1977 is the date on which paragraphs (a) and (b)(i) and (c)(i) test whether the person was a pensioner.
-- src:99 | (i) on July 1, 1977 was not a pensioner but had attained twenty-five years of age and resided in Canada or, if that person did not reside in Canada, had resided in Canada for any period after attaining eighteen years of age or possessed a valid immigration visa,
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(1)(b)(i) (src:99)
`s 3(1): July 1, 1977` MEANS YearMonthDay 1977 7 1

-- s 3(1)(a): "every person who was a pensioner on July 1, 1977"
-- src:97 | (a) every person who was a pensioner on July 1, 1977;
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(1)(a) (src:97)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 3: Facts of age and residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(a): the person was a pensioner on July 1, 1977` facts MEANS
    `the person is a pensioner` (facts's `the person's application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977`)

-- s 3(1)(b)(i): on July 1, 1977 not a pensioner, but 25 or older, and resident in Canada or, failing that, with some
-- earlier residence after eighteen or a valid immigration visa.
-- src:99 | (i) on July 1, 1977 was not a pensioner but had attained twenty-five years of age and resided in Canada or, if that person did not reside in Canada, had resided in Canada for any period after attaining eighteen years of age or possessed a valid immigration visa,
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(1)(b)(i) (src:99)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 3: Facts of age and residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(b)(i): on July 1, 1977 the person was not a pensioner but had attained twenty-five years of age and met the test of residence` facts MEANS
        NOT (`the person is a pensioner` (facts's `the person's application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977`))
    AND ((`the age in complete years on` (`s 3(1): July 1, 1977`) `of a person born on` (facts's `the date of birth`)) AT LEAST 25)
    AND (    facts's `resided in Canada on July 1, 1977`
          OR (    (NOT (facts's `resided in Canada on July 1, 1977`))
              AND (    facts's `had resided in Canada for any period after attaining eighteen years of age`
                    OR facts's `possessed a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977`)))

-- "has attained sixty-five years of age", at the day of approval (fork OA1-F1). One rule; ss 3(1)(c)(ii) and 3(2)(a)
-- say the same thing and call it.
-- src:100 | (ii) has attained sixty-five years of age, and
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(1)(b)(ii) (src:100)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 3: Facts of age and residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(b)(ii): the person has attained sixty-five years of age` facts MEANS
    (`the age in complete years on` (facts's `the day on which the person's application is approved`) `of a person born on` (facts's `the date of birth`)) AT LEAST 65

-- s 3(1)(b)(iii): resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding the day of approval or, if not, present for
-- an aggregate period at least three times the aggregate absences during those ten years, and resided in Canada for at
-- least one year immediately preceding. The "and has resided ... at least one year" is read as belonging to the second
-- limb (fork OA1-F2); it makes no difference when a person who resided ten years has also resided one.
-- src:101 | (iii) has resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding the day on which that person’s application is approved or, if that person has not so resided, has, after attaining eighteen years of age, been present in Canada prior to those ten years for an aggregate period at least equal to three times the aggregate periods of absence from Canada during those ten years, and has resided in Canada for at least one year immediately preceding the day on which that person’s application is approved; and
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(1)(b)(iii) (src:101)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 3: Facts of age and residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(b)(iii): the person has resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding, or has been present for three times the absences and resided for one year` facts MEANS
        facts's `resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding the day on which the person's application is approved`
    OR  (    (NOT (facts's `resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding the day on which the person's application is approved`))
         AND (facts's `aggregate period of presence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, prior to those ten years`
                  AT LEAST (3 TIMES (facts's `aggregate periods of absence from Canada during those ten years`)))
         AND facts's `resided in Canada for at least one year immediately preceding the day on which the person's application is approved`)

-- s 3(1)(b): all three of (i), (ii) and (iii)
-- src:98 | (b) every person who
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(1)(b) (src:98)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 3: Facts of age and residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(b): the person is qualified for a full monthly pension under paragraph (b)` facts MEANS
        `s 3(1)(b)(i): on July 1, 1977 the person was not a pensioner but had attained twenty-five years of age and met the test of residence` facts
    AND `s 3(1)(b)(ii): the person has attained sixty-five years of age` facts
    AND `s 3(1)(b)(iii): the person has resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding, or has been present for three times the absences and resided for one year` facts

-- s 3(1)(c): not a pensioner on July 1, 1977, 65 or older, and at least forty years of residence after eighteen.
-- src:102 | (c) every person who
-- src:103 | (i) was not a pensioner on July 1, 1977,
-- src:104 | (ii) has attained sixty-five years of age, and
-- src:105 | (iii) has resided in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which that person’s application is approved for an aggregate period of at least forty years.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(1)(c) (src:102-105)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 3: Facts of age and residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(c): the person is qualified for a full monthly pension under paragraph (c)` facts MEANS
        NOT (`the person is a pensioner` (facts's `the person's application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977`))
    AND `s 3(1)(b)(ii): the person has attained sixty-five years of age` facts
    AND (facts's `aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the person's application is approved` AT LEAST 40)

-- src:95 | Payment of full pension
-- src:96 | 3 (1) Subject to this Act and the regulations, a full monthly pension may be paid to
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(1) (src:95-96)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 3: Facts of age and residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1): a full monthly pension may be paid to the person` facts MEANS
        `s 3(1)(a): the person was a pensioner on July 1, 1977` facts
    OR  `s 3(1)(b): the person is qualified for a full monthly pension under paragraph (b)` facts
    OR  `s 3(1)(c): the person is qualified for a full monthly pension under paragraph (c)` facts

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 3(2): who may be paid a partial monthly pension

-- src:108 | (a) has attained sixty-five years of age; and
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(2)(a) (src:108)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 3: Facts of age and residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(2)(a): the person has attained sixty-five years of age` facts MEANS
    `s 3(1)(b)(ii): the person has attained sixty-five years of age` facts

-- s 3(2)(b): at least ten but less than forty years of residence after eighteen, and, if less than twenty, resident in
-- Canada on the day preceding the day of approval (fork OA1-F3: the aggregate period is tested unrounded; s 3(4) rounds it only for the amount).
-- src:109 | (b) has resided in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which that person’s application is approved for an aggregate period of at least ten years but less than forty years and, where that aggregate period is less than twenty years, was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which that person’s application is approved.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(2)(b) (src:109)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 3: Facts of age and residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(2)(b): the person has resided in Canada for at least ten but less than forty years and, if less than twenty, was resident on the day preceding` facts MEANS
        (facts's `aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the person's application is approved` AT LEAST 10)
    AND (facts's `aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the person's application is approved` LESS THAN 40)
    AND (    (facts's `aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the person's application is approved` AT LEAST 20)
          OR facts's `was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the person's application is approved`)

-- src:106 | Payment of partial pension
-- src:107 | (2) Subject to this Act and the regulations, a partial monthly pension may be paid for any month in a payment quarter to every person who is not eligible for a full monthly pension under subsection (1) and
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 3(2) (src:106-107)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 3: Facts of age and residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(2): a partial monthly pension may be paid to the person` facts MEANS
        NOT (`s 3(1): a full monthly pension may be paid to the person` facts)
    AND `s 3(2)(a): the person has attained sixty-five years of age` facts
    AND `s 3(2)(b): the person has resided in Canada for at least ten but less than forty years and, if less than twenty, was resident on the day preceding` facts

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 4(1): legal residence

-- src:116 | Residence in Canada must be or have been legal
-- src:117 | 4 (1) A person who was not a pensioner on July 1, 1977 is eligible for a pension under this Part only if
-- src:118 | (a) on the day preceding the day on which that person’s application is approved that person is a Canadian citizen or, if not, is legally resident in Canada; or
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 4(1)(a) (src:116-118)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(1)(a): on the day preceding the day of approval the person is a Canadian citizen or, if not, legally resident in Canada` facts MEANS
        facts's `on the day preceding the day on which the person's application is approved, the person is a Canadian citizen`
    OR  facts's `on the day preceding the day on which the person's application is approved, the person is legally resident in Canada`

-- src:119 | (b) on the day preceding the day that person ceased to reside in Canada that person was a Canadian citizen or, if not, was legally resident in Canada.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 4(1)(b) (src:119)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(1)(b): on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was a Canadian citizen or, if not, legally resident` facts MEANS
        facts's `the person has ceased to reside in Canada`
    AND (    facts's `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada, the person was a Canadian citizen`
          OR facts's `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada, the person was legally resident in Canada`)

-- "A person who was not a pensioner on July 1, 1977 is eligible for a pension under this Part only if (a) or (b)":
-- a person who was a pensioner on July 1, 1977 is not held to the requirement.
-- src:116 | Residence in Canada must be or have been legal
-- src:117 | 4 (1) A person who was not a pensioner on July 1, 1977 is eligible for a pension under this Part only if
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 4(1) (src:116-117)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(1): the person meets the requirement of legal residence for a pension under this Part` facts MEANS
        `the person is a pensioner` (facts's `the person's application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977`)
    OR  `s 4(1)(a): on the day preceding the day of approval the person is a Canadian citizen or, if not, legally resident in Canada` facts
    OR  `s 4(1)(b): on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was a Canadian citizen or, if not, legally resident` facts

