-- s 4.1: the presumption that follows an intended waiver. The "prescribed information" is Regulations ss 21(8) and
-- 22(2) (piece oa3): the person-side fact is whether the information the Minister has includes it.

-- src:122 | Presumption
-- src:123 | 4.1 If the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of a person under subsection 5(4) and the information available to the Minister under this Act with respect to that person includes the prescribed information, the person is presumed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, to have met the requirements of
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 4.1 (src:122-123)
GIVEN `the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of the person under subsection 5(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 21(8) (piece oa3); section 22(2) (piece oa3): Regulations, "prescribed information"
      `the information available to the Minister under this Act with respect to the person includes the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4.1: the presumption applies` `the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of the person under subsection 5(4)` `the information available to the Minister under this Act with respect to the person includes the prescribed information` MEANS
        `the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of the person under subsection 5(4)`
    AND `the information available to the Minister under this Act with respect to the person includes the prescribed information`

-- src:123 | 4.1 If the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of a person under subsection 5(4) and the information available to the Minister under this Act with respect to that person includes the prescribed information, the person is presumed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, to have met the requirements of
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 4.1 (src:123)
GIVEN `the presumption of section 4.1 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4.1: the person is presumed to have met the requirements` `the presumption of section 4.1 applies` `there is evidence to the contrary` MEANS
        `the presumption of section 4.1 applies`
    AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)

-- src:124 | (a) subparagraph 3(1)(b)(iii) or (c)(iii) or paragraph 3(2)(b); or
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 4.1(a) (src:124)
GIVEN `the person actually meets subparagraph 3(1)(b)(iii) or (c)(iii) or paragraph 3(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is presumed to have met the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4.1(a): the requirement of subparagraph 3(1)(b)(iii) or (c)(iii) or paragraph 3(2)(b) is treated as met` `the person actually meets subparagraph 3(1)(b)(iii) or (c)(iii) or paragraph 3(2)(b)` `the person is presumed to have met the requirements` MEANS
        `the person actually meets subparagraph 3(1)(b)(iii) or (c)(iii) or paragraph 3(2)(b)`
    OR  `the person is presumed to have met the requirements`

-- src:125 | (b) paragraph 4(1)(a) or (b).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 4.1(b) (src:125)
GIVEN `the person actually meets paragraph 4(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is presumed to have met the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4.1(b): the requirement of paragraph 4(1)(a) or (b) is treated as met` `the person actually meets paragraph 4(1)(a) or (b)` `the person is presumed to have met the requirements` MEANS
        `the person actually meets paragraph 4(1)(a) or (b)`
    OR  `the person is presumed to have met the requirements`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5(1): qualified, applied and approved; no payment for a period before the day of approval

-- src:126 | Limitations
-- src:127 | 5 (1) No pension may be paid to any person unless that person is qualified under subsection 3(1) or (2), an application therefor has been made by or on behalf of that person and the application has been approved, and, except as provided in this Act, no pension may be paid to any person in respect of any period prior to the day on which that person’s application is approved.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(1) (src:126-127)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 3: Facts of age and residence`
      `an application for a pension has been made by or on behalf of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(1): a pension may be paid to the person` facts `an application for a pension has been made by or on behalf of the person` `the application has been approved` MEANS
        (   `s 3(1): a full monthly pension may be paid to the person` facts
         OR `s 3(2): a partial monthly pension may be paid to the person` facts)
    AND `an application for a pension has been made by or on behalf of the person`
    AND `the application has been approved`

-- "except as provided in this Act, no pension may be paid to any person in respect of any period prior to the day on
-- which that person's application is approved": a day before the day of approval is payable only if another provision
-- of the Act allows it (ss 8(1), 8(2), 28.1, 29, 30, 32 are the provisions that do) (fork OA1-F17 of NOTES.md).
-- src:127 | 5 (1) No pension may be paid to any person unless that person is qualified under subsection 3(1) or (2), an application therefor has been made by or on behalf of that person and the application has been approved, and, except as provided in this Act, no pension may be paid to any person in respect of any period prior to the day on which that person’s application is approved.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(1), second limb (src:127)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      approval IS A DATE
      `another provision of the Act allows payment in respect of that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(1): a pension may be paid in respect of the day` day approval `another provision of the Act allows payment in respect of that day` MEANS
        day AT LEAST approval
    OR  `another provision of the Act allows payment in respect of that day`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5(2): an application deemed on the day the person reaches 65 when an allowance ceases for that reason

-- src:128 | Application deemed to have been made and approved
-- src:129 | (2) Where an allowance ceases to be payable to a person by reason of that person having reached sixty-five years of age, the Minister may deem an application under subsection (1) to have been made by that person and approved, on the day on which the person reached that age.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(2) (src:128-129)
GIVEN `an allowance ceases to be payable to the person by reason of the person having reached sixty-five years of age` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 19 (piece oa2); section 21 (piece oa2): when an allowance ceases to be payable
      `the Minister deems an application under subsection 5(1) to have been made and approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2): the application is deemed to have been made and approved` `an allowance ceases to be payable to the person by reason of the person having reached sixty-five years of age` `the Minister deems an application under subsection 5(1) to have been made and approved` MEANS
        `an allowance ceases to be payable to the person by reason of the person having reached sixty-five years of age`
    AND `the Minister deems an application under subsection 5(1) to have been made and approved`

-- The day on which the deemed application is made and approved: "the day on which the person reached that age".
-- src:129 | (2) Where an allowance ceases to be payable to a person by reason of that person having reached sixty-five years of age, the Minister may deem an application under subsection (1) to have been made by that person and approved, on the day on which the person reached that age.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(2) (src:129)
GIVEN birth IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 5(2): the day on which the person reached sixty-five years of age` birth MEANS
    `the day on which a person born on` birth `attains the age of` 65

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5(3): incarcerated persons. This answers the register input
-- `the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` that piece oa2 takes at ss 19(1.1) and 22(1).

-- src:132 | (a) that is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of any Act of Parliament; or
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(3)(a) (src:132)
GIVEN sentence IS A `Sentence of imprisonment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(3)(a): the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` sentence MEANS
    sentence's `to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament`

-- src:133 | (b) that exceeds 90 days and is to be served in a prison, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act, if the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(3)(b) (src:133)
GIVEN sentence IS A `Sentence of imprisonment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(3)(b): the sentence exceeds 90 days and is to be served in a prison, the province having agreed` sentence MEANS
        (sentence's `length in days` GREATER THAN 90)
    AND sentence's `to be served in a prison as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act`
    AND sentence's `the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act`

-- src:131 | (3) No pension may be paid in respect of a period of incarceration — exclusive of the first month of that period — to a person who is subject to a sentence of imprisonment
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(3) (src:131)
GIVEN `the person is incarcerated` IS A BOOLEAN
      sentence IS A `Sentence of imprisonment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(3): the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` `the person is incarcerated` sentence MEANS
        `the person is incarcerated`
    AND (    `s 5(3)(a): the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` sentence
          OR `s 5(3)(b): the sentence exceeds 90 days and is to be served in a prison, the province having agreed` sentence)

-- "No pension may be paid in respect of a period of incarceration -- exclusive of the first month of that period":
-- the months barred run from the month after the first month of the period to the month before the month of
-- release (the month of release is paid, once the Minister is notified: ss 8(2.1) and 9.2) (fork OA1-F4 of NOTES.md).
-- src:130 | Incarcerated persons
-- src:131 | (3) No pension may be paid in respect of a period of incarceration — exclusive of the first month of that period — to a person who is subject to a sentence of imprisonment
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5(3) (src:130-131)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the period of incarceration began` IS A DATE
      -- out of range: section 2 (piece oas-g0): "release", the keel's definition
      `the day on which the person was released` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(3): no pension may be paid for the month` month `the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` `the day on which the period of incarceration began` `the day on which the person was released` MEANS
        `the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)`
    AND (`the first day of the month containing` month GREATER THAN `the first day of the month containing` `the day on which the period of incarceration began`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the day on which the person was released`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST released THEN `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN `the first day of the month containing` released)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5.1: withdrawal of an application

-- "at any time before payment of the pension commences": strictly before the day on which payment commences (fork OA1-F19 of NOTES.md).
-- src:144 | Withdrawal of application
-- src:145 | 5.1 (1) An applicant may withdraw an application for a pension by giving a written notice of their withdrawal to the Minister at any time before payment of the pension commences.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5.1(1) (src:144-145)
GIVEN `the applicant gives the Minister a written notice of their withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the day on which payment of the pension commences` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5.1(1): the applicant may withdraw the application` `the applicant gives the Minister a written notice of their withdrawal` `the day on which the notice is given` `the day on which payment of the pension commences` MEANS
        `the applicant gives the Minister a written notice of their withdrawal`
    AND (`the day on which the notice is given` LESS THAN `the day on which payment of the pension commences`)

-- "shall not after that time be used": before the withdrawal the application may still be used; after it, not.
-- src:146 | Effect of withdrawal
-- src:147 | (2) If an application for a pension is withdrawn under subsection (1), the withdrawn application shall not after that time be used for the purpose of determining the applicant’s eligibility for a pension.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 5.1(2) (src:146-147)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application was withdrawn` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5.1(2): the application may be used to determine the applicant's eligibility on the day` day `the day on which the application was withdrawn` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the application was withdrawn`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST withdrawn THEN day AT MOST withdrawn

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 6: the Minister's access to census ages (fork OA1-F5 of NOTES.md: "more than thirty years before" is strict)

-- src:149 | Information from Statistics Canada
-- src:150 | Census statistics
-- src:151 | 6 Subject to the conditions specified in the regulations, the Minister is entitled, for the purpose of ascertaining the age of any pensioner or any applicant for a pension, to obtain from Statistics Canada, on request, any information respecting the age of a pensioner or applicant that is contained in the returns of any census taken more than thirty years before the date of the request.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 6 (src:149-151)
GIVEN `the information respects the age of a pensioner or of an applicant for a pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is contained in the returns of a census` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the census was taken` IS A DATE
      `the date of the request` IS A DATE
      -- out of range: section 18.1 (piece oa3): Regulations
      `the conditions specified in the regulations are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6: the Minister is entitled to obtain the information from Statistics Canada on request` `the information respects the age of a pensioner or of an applicant for a pension` `the information is contained in the returns of a census` `the day on which the census was taken` `the date of the request` `the conditions specified in the regulations are met` MEANS
        `the conditions specified in the regulations are met`
    AND `the information respects the age of a pensioner or of an applicant for a pension`
    AND `the information is contained in the returns of a census`
    AND (`add years` `the day on which the census was taken` 30 LESS THAN `the date of the request`)
